      3  10000 ????						; ==============================================================================
      4  10000 ????						; savior kernel — HERO-style fixed-time rendering kernel
      5  10000 ????						; ==============================================================================
      6  10000 ????						; A from-scratch Atari 2600 kernel modeled after Activision's HERO.
      7  10000 ????						;
      8  10000 ????						; Architecture:
      9  10000 ????						;   - 4K ROM at $F000-$FFFF (no bankswitching)
     10  10000 ????						;   - Kernel renders 192 visible scanlines: 144 cave + 48 HUD
     11  10000 ????						;   - Cave: 3 tile rows × 48 scanlines each
     12  10000 ????						;   - Reflected playfield (CTRLPF D0=1) — symmetric cave
     13  10000 ????						;   - GRP0 = player (square sprite), GRP1 = future objects
     14  10000 ????						;   - Per-scanline kernel with WSYNC for stable timing
     15  10000 ????						;   - PF registers written ONCE per tile row (TIA persists)
     16  10000 ????						;   - Overscan: input handling + game logic
     17  10000 ????						;
     18  10000 ????						; Frame timing (262 scanlines @ 60Hz NTSC):
     19  10000 ????						;   VSYNC     3 lines
     20  10000 ????						;   VBLANK   37 lines	(game logic + positioning)
     21  10000 ????						;   Kernel  192 lines	(144 cave + 48 HUD)
     22  10000 ????						;   Overscan  30 lines (input + movement)
     23  10000 ????						;   Total   262 lines
     24  10000 ????						;
     25  10000 ????						; Key difference from naive kernels:
     26  10000 ????						;   The inner .Line loop is UNCONDITIONAL — no per-scanline branches for
     27  10000 ????						;   sprite visibility. The player check uses a compare+branch that costs
     28  10000 ????						;   16c (off-screen) or 19c (on-screen), both well within the 76-cycle
     29  10000 ????						;   budget. PF registers are written once per tile row, not per scanline.
     30  10000 ????						; ==============================================================================
     31  10000 ????
